00:44:14.584 --> 00:44:19.508
Uh, with AI generating more code
themes and even entire websites, do

00:44:19.508 --> 00:44:22.989
you think that accessibility bugs
are gonna become better or worse?

00:44:23.046 --> 00:44:25.519
I'm assuming as far as, like,
volume and severity goes.

00:44:26.808 --> 00:44:30.272
Oh, yeah, that, that's a good question,
uh, because, you know, uh, actually

00:44:30.272 --> 00:44:34.469
in, in the… Every developer is using
AI, every person using AI right now.

00:44:34.471 --> 00:44:38.644
But I think to go directly with the
question, I think it's probably both,

00:44:39.074 --> 00:44:44.038
because AI can help the developer
to catch the problem early, explain

00:44:44.042 --> 00:44:48.348
the accessibility requirement, uh,
generate the better markup and great

00:44:48.374 --> 00:44:50.029
test, and also review all the codes.

00:44:50.029 --> 00:44:55.631
So, uh, the, the problem here is
when AI start creating a enormous

00:44:55.656 --> 00:44:57.134
amount of code very quick.

00:44:57.551 --> 00:45:02.621
So th- this mean that the assumption of
the AI can reproduce a much large problem.

00:45:02.681 --> 00:45:08.415
So, uh, for example, if you create,
um, a, a button or an interaction with

00:45:08.415 --> 00:45:13.670
the AI and you don't give the exact
information, uh, on what is the behavior,

00:45:14.031 --> 00:45:16.296
you, you will have a big problem on it.

00:45:16.337 --> 00:45:22.098
But I think the in- interesting chance
here with the AI is the, is speed,

00:45:22.252 --> 00:45:24.915
uh, uh, becoming a less problem.

00:45:25.077 --> 00:45:26.808
I, I don't think the AI is a bottleneck.

00:45:27.227 --> 00:45:30.616
I think it, it depend
how you handle the AI.

00:45:31.673 --> 00:45:32.438
I think so, yeah.

00:45:34.447 --> 00:45:35.145
All right, cool.

00:45:35.616 --> 00:45:38.401
Um, yeah, so it sounds like
