00:45:59.016 --> 00:46:02.964
Oh, well, uh, I, I I think this is
a common problem that most of the

00:46:02.967 --> 00:46:05.752
people have when, when I'm working
with, with, you know, I mean,

00:46:05.752 --> 00:46:07.703
existing projects or even new project.

00:46:08.203 --> 00:46:12.770
Be- but I think probably one of the
harder part, uh, is inside the, the,

00:46:12.785 --> 00:46:18.594
the project because the plan probably
can change, the priority can move, and

00:46:18.603 --> 00:46:23.218
the management will sometimes, uh, push
for something completely different.

00:46:23.640 --> 00:46:29.002
Um, for me, I think the key is not trying
to protect the whole plan at all cost.

00:46:29.518 --> 00:46:33.794
Uh, I try to, to protect more
like, uh, you know, taking the, the

00:46:33.794 --> 00:46:35.974
important things that I can fix.

00:46:36.271 --> 00:46:43.329
Um, I always ask, uh, I'm, I, I alwa- I
always say my- myself, like, "I can't,

00:46:43.459 --> 00:46:48.580
I cannot fix everything now, but at
least I'm going to fix this, and I'm

00:46:48.583 --> 00:46:50.544
assuming the risk of, of doing it."

00:46:50.552 --> 00:46:55.628
So, um, I think the, uh, avoiding
the, the, the, the problem is worse.

00:46:55.639 --> 00:47:01.075
But so if you keep the small improvement
and divisible instead of letting it

00:47:01.101 --> 00:47:04.695
disappear completely, I think you
have something, uh, to, to work with.

00:47:04.695 --> 00:47:10.472
So sometimes accessibility, uh,
works, uh, need to adapt to the

00:47:10.474 --> 00:47:14.245
business, so like, you know, like
everything else inside the, the page.

00:47:14.274 --> 00:47:19.716
But I think a- adapting doesn't have to
be like abandoning the idea or abandoning

00:47:19.718 --> 00:47:21.294
the plan or, or the website itself.

