00:47:30.718 --> 00:47:34.939
Um, so on one of your later slides,
you mentioned six potential sources

00:47:34.939 --> 00:47:38.236
of change when it comes to, like,
how the WordPress experience is

00:47:38.236 --> 00:47:42.232
delivered, and they were core updates,
theme updates, plugin updates- Mm-hmm

00:47:42.232 --> 00:47:46.216
global style edits, new content,
and then remote widget changes.

00:47:46.250 --> 00:47:49.450
And you even said, like, with the
remote widget changes, um, that

00:47:49.450 --> 00:47:52.337
can happen without any sort of
intentional action from the people

00:47:52.337 --> 00:47:53.555
that actually own the website.

00:47:53.968 --> 00:47:57.665
So my question with that context is, in
your experience, are changes that come

00:47:57.665 --> 00:48:02.613
from outside of the team itself of equal
risk to accessibility deterioration, so

00:48:02.613 --> 00:48:07.189
those sort of updates that happen, um,
that the team doesn't do themselves, or is

00:48:07.191 --> 00:48:10.176
it sort of like one of those six sources
is the one that you see as, like, the

00:48:10.176 --> 00:48:12.596
primary risk or, like, worse than others?

00:48:12.611 --> 00:48:14.310
Well, yeah.

00:48:14.524 --> 00:48:19.756
Yeah, th- that… It… A thing is, is,
is, uh, is a common to, to happen in, in

00:48:19.759 --> 00:48:23.250
every WordPress because when you have,
for example, let's, let's say that you

00:48:23.254 --> 00:48:28.497
have the option to auto-update all the
plugins, um, you can't control that.

00:48:28.517 --> 00:48:31.301
You don't have the control
on that when you are with the

00:48:31.316 --> 00:48:33.375
plugin itself is start updating.

00:48:33.573 --> 00:48:36.884
And even if you have the control,
like, you are doing something

00:48:36.884 --> 00:48:39.482
new, uh, in, in a… Do you know?

00:48:39.488 --> 00:48:42.638
Like, for example, th- that happened
to me in, in my actual work.

00:48:42.859 --> 00:48:49.178
Like, we make up, uh, our custom plugin,
um, we make that plugin, like, two

00:48:49.189 --> 00:48:53.136
version before the, the new release
of the WordPress, so we say, "Yeah,

00:48:53.321 --> 00:48:55.015
we are gonna update that later."

00:48:56.142 --> 00:49:01.209
And, you know, we, we have two majors
update, uh, behind in, in that plugin,

00:49:01.209 --> 00:49:05.725
and so the, the, the, uh, the moment
we, we do the update of the plugin,

00:49:05.792 --> 00:49:08.381
everything's go down in the page.

00:49:08.410 --> 00:49:13.669
So you know, it's like a, like a little
emergency we have inside the work.

00:49:13.673 --> 00:49:17.091
But again, you know, it, it is, it's
not something that you can control

00:49:17.091 --> 00:49:21.490
itself because- Sometimes you,
you are going to broke something

00:49:21.491 --> 00:49:23.089
inside the WordPress installation.

00:49:23.154 --> 00:49:27.842
Uh, any plugin is going to go
down or e- even, uh, CSS can broke

00:49:27.857 --> 00:49:29.622
all the, the, the, the behavior.

00:49:29.919 --> 00:49:35.851
But I think that, you know, like all the
things that give you WordPress to work

00:49:35.877 --> 00:49:39.663
with, like you, you can do everything
inside WordPress, and I think that is

00:49:39.701 --> 00:49:44.726
overwhelming when you are, like, doing a
project, doing a plugin, or working on a

00:49:44.764 --> 00:49:47.898
page, uh, i- in, in, in every WordPress.

00:49:48.166 --> 00:49:54.068
So I think that you need to make,
make, like, the internal decision

00:49:54.077 --> 00:49:57.955
like, "Okay, I'm going to fix this,
I'm going to update this, but I'm

00:49:57.961 --> 00:50:00.321
taking the risk on everything." Yeah.

00:50:01.236 --> 00:50:01.715
Okay, yeah.

00:50:01.775 --> 00:50:05.452
So just get ready, be prepared whenever
